WEBVTT

00:00:13.680 --> 00:00:16.530
Nothing feels better than the 
air in your own hometown!

00:00:16.900 --> 00:00:17.610
Let's go.

00:00:24.040 --> 00:00:25.580
Wait up!

00:00:24.160 --> 00:00:27.170
March 28 15:02

00:00:25.580 --> 00:00:27.170
You're too slow!

00:00:28.370 --> 00:00:30.420
Back home for the first 
time in three years...

00:00:30.910 --> 00:00:32.650
It hasn't changed a bit!

00:00:32.650 --> 00:00:37.220
Hang on. If we're being specific,
that "three years" is more like 27 years.

00:00:37.440 --> 00:00:39.660
For starters, you left your 
hometown of Couljours at age 12,

00:00:39.660 --> 00:00:42.840
and trained to become a dealer at 
a casino to keep yourself fed.

00:00:42.840 --> 00:00:43.980
After learning how to deal cards,

00:00:43.980 --> 00:00:46.400
you joined the Horologue-killing 
organization Chronos at age 20,

00:00:46.400 --> 00:00:48.060
where you met Aisrehdar and the agent—

00:00:48.060 --> 00:00:49.320
Okay, okay.

00:00:49.320 --> 00:00:51.570
Girls don't like guys who nitpick, you know.

00:00:52.810 --> 00:00:56.510
It's in a remote location more than 
half a day's travel from the airport.

00:00:57.110 --> 00:01:00.240
There aren't any businesses or 
famous buildings to speak of.

00:01:00.970 --> 00:01:04.760
It's just a small rural town 
with a beautiful view.

00:01:04.760 --> 00:01:05.850
That's Couljours.

00:01:05.850 --> 00:01:09.750
Sheesh, I'm glad we landed in 
a place that was close to it.

00:01:10.050 --> 00:01:13.120
Darling, I want something cold to drink!

00:01:13.120 --> 00:01:15.580
Good grief, you two...

00:01:15.580 --> 00:01:17.760
Oh, it's Old Lady Kate's bakery!

00:01:17.760 --> 00:01:19.460
So it's still in business!

00:01:21.870 --> 00:01:24.620
The game machine next to the
general store! That takes me back!

00:01:24.620 --> 00:01:27.020
I had the high score on this thing!

00:01:29.160 --> 00:01:30.360
All right!

00:01:30.360 --> 00:01:33.810
Witness the techniques of the guy 
they called "Sixteen Straight Wins"!

00:01:35.670 --> 00:01:36.320
Huh?

00:01:39.470 --> 00:01:41.670
That place with the nasty 
steak is hanging in there.

00:01:41.670 --> 00:01:43.910
And here's its whiny spokesdog, Buttller!

00:01:44.980 --> 00:01:48.350
Or are you his grandson?
Every generation is just like the last.

00:01:48.350 --> 00:01:50.460
Oh? You wanna fight?

00:01:50.700 --> 00:01:54.000
They called me "Flashing Mad Dog."

00:01:56.290 --> 00:01:58.490
Audacious, aren't ya? You wanna go?!

00:01:59.410 --> 00:02:00.680
Darling!

00:02:00.960 --> 00:02:03.860
Since we're here, I'd love 
to meet your parents.

00:02:04.230 --> 00:02:07.400
Sadly, they've both passed away.

00:02:07.400 --> 00:02:10.960
Oh, really? I didn't know.

00:02:10.960 --> 00:02:12.570
Don't worry about it.

00:02:12.570 --> 00:02:14.700
It was 27 years ago.

00:02:15.260 --> 00:02:16.770
I'm sorry.

00:02:16.770 --> 00:02:19.930
Well, then... do you think 
we could visit their graves?

00:02:19.480 --> 00:02:21.140
Stop! Stop it!

00:02:19.930 --> 00:02:21.410
Sure, later.

00:02:22.130 --> 00:02:23.160
<i>What is it?</i>

00:02:23.940 --> 00:02:25.600
<i>Something's bothering me...</i>

00:02:26.320 --> 00:02:30.010
Well, just reminiscing 
won't get us anywhere.

00:02:30.410 --> 00:02:32.290
Let's start by investigating my past.

00:02:32.600 --> 00:02:36.530
Hey! Isn't this where your last mission was?

00:02:36.530 --> 00:02:37.770
Whoa!

00:02:38.340 --> 00:02:39.540
Watch it, you!

00:02:39.540 --> 00:02:40.880
Sorry!

00:02:41.420 --> 00:02:43.360
Auntie!

00:02:44.610 --> 00:02:46.890
I drew this! Look!

00:02:47.110 --> 00:02:49.670
No need to rush. Let me have a look.

00:02:51.430 --> 00:02:54.920
My, it's a lovely drawing!

00:02:54.920 --> 00:02:58.030
I'm sure you'll be a wonderful 
artist when you grow up.

00:03:02.380 --> 00:03:04.080
Hey, Victor...

00:03:04.080 --> 00:03:05.370
What are you doing?

00:03:09.400 --> 00:03:10.550
Mom...

00:03:12.840 --> 00:03:15.570
"Mom"? What are you saying?

00:03:17.130 --> 00:03:18.380
Hold it there.

00:03:18.380 --> 00:03:19.550
Look at that runny nose.

00:03:19.730 --> 00:03:20.920
Got a cold?

00:03:20.920 --> 00:03:22.800
It's definitely a cold.

00:03:23.880 --> 00:03:25.430
Let me take a look at you.

00:03:25.770 --> 00:03:28.680
No! I don't have a cold!

00:03:26.760 --> 00:03:28.680
Don't fuss, now.

00:03:29.410 --> 00:03:30.600
No!

00:03:31.430 --> 00:03:32.610
You don't mean that's...

00:03:45.120 --> 00:03:46.200
Darling, look!

00:03:47.920 --> 00:03:49.700
Thirty-four years ago?!

00:03:56.720 --> 00:03:57.340
<i>That's it.</i>

00:03:58.730 --> 00:04:01.840
<i>It was this town's odd nostalgic 
feel that was bothering me.</i>

00:04:02.810 --> 00:04:04.220
<i>It's old, but new...</i>

00:04:05.120 --> 00:04:06.970
<i>New, but old.</i>

00:04:06.970 --> 00:04:08.860
I don't want a shot!

00:04:08.860 --> 00:04:11.390
Come, now, it won't hurt...

00:04:09.710 --> 00:04:11.030
Oh, dear.

00:04:11.030 --> 00:04:13.570
<i>Are they really Victor's parents?</i>

00:04:11.390 --> 00:04:14.040
It's all right. Don't be scared.

00:04:14.040 --> 00:04:15.230
<i>No way.</i>

00:04:15.680 --> 00:04:20.420
<i>But if we assume they are, 
there's only one possibility.</i>

00:04:22.530 --> 00:04:24.070
<i>Time has turned backwards.</i>

00:05:56.940 --> 00:06:01.040
Save me, Auntie! I don't want a shot!

00:05:58.980 --> 00:06:01.040
If we've gone back to the past,

00:06:01.560 --> 00:06:04.980
when did it happen, and how? What caused it?

00:06:04.980 --> 00:06:07.550
Nothing seemed wrong when 
we walked into this town.

00:06:08.470 --> 00:06:12.520
You said Victor left the 
countryside at age 12, right?

00:06:12.520 --> 00:06:17.770
That was 27 years ago, and where 
we are now is 34 years back.

00:06:17.770 --> 00:06:21.120
Wait, so how old is the Victor 
who's in this town now?

00:06:21.710 --> 00:06:23.510
Darling, are you okay?

00:06:28.570 --> 00:06:30.210
I never thought I'd see you again.

00:06:30.850 --> 00:06:33.510
There, there. Don't cry, now.

00:06:35.390 --> 00:06:36.790
Huh? You...

00:06:36.790 --> 00:06:40.690
You're very pale!

00:06:41.060 --> 00:06:42.210
Are you all right?

00:06:42.620 --> 00:06:43.880
Are you a patient?

00:06:44.520 --> 00:06:46.900
If you'd like an examination, we can talk.

00:06:46.900 --> 00:06:48.880
Eve, get things ready for an exam.

00:06:49.380 --> 00:06:50.860
Yes, dear.

00:06:51.230 --> 00:06:54.110
No, wait! Please, listen to—

00:06:54.990 --> 00:06:58.100
Victor, open your eyes. 
This town isn't right.

00:06:58.580 --> 00:07:02.560
Aren't you always saying that 
time never turns backwards?

00:07:04.930 --> 00:07:08.810
What's the matter?
You seem quite out of sorts.

00:07:10.350 --> 00:07:13.020
Oh, you certainly are pale!

00:07:13.020 --> 00:07:15.990
Yes, I, Alexander Putin, 
should examine you—

00:07:15.990 --> 00:07:20.330
He's fine! He's just a little 
tired from our long journey.

00:07:21.290 --> 00:07:23.290
We'll go rest in our hotel.

00:07:35.530 --> 00:07:36.390
It's no use.

00:07:37.070 --> 00:07:38.240
He won't answer.

00:07:39.140 --> 00:07:42.720
I was hoping to ask Snake 
if he had any leads.

00:07:42.720 --> 00:07:47.010
Jeez, why do we have to 
sleep in a place like this?

00:07:47.010 --> 00:07:50.070
At least let me stay at 
a hotel with my darling!

00:07:50.290 --> 00:07:51.890
Don't complain.

00:07:51.890 --> 00:07:53.620
Until we know what's going on,

00:07:53.620 --> 00:07:56.020
we should avoid contact with 
the people of this town.

00:07:56.020 --> 00:07:59.580
Stingy Kiri! Father disrespecter! Virgin!

00:08:00.220 --> 00:08:02.100
Virginity has nothing to do with this!

00:08:02.100 --> 00:08:05.480
Twelve plus 27 minus 34 is...

00:08:05.480 --> 00:08:06.840
First, the 12...

00:08:07.510 --> 00:08:10.680
Until we can prove that this 
isn't the work of a Horologue,

00:08:10.680 --> 00:08:12.110
we need to stay alert.

00:08:12.110 --> 00:08:14.070
We'll start investigating in the morning.

00:08:14.550 --> 00:08:17.030
We can rotate the watch every 
two hours. Okay, Victor?

00:08:18.340 --> 00:08:19.200
Victor!

00:08:19.650 --> 00:08:21.600
Oh, right. Sure.

00:08:21.910 --> 00:08:25.190
After two hours, you'll eat 
pasta through your nose, right?

00:08:25.190 --> 00:08:26.110
Wrong!

00:08:26.440 --> 00:08:27.950
I'm talking about the watch!

00:08:27.950 --> 00:08:31.030
Honestly, am I the only 
one being cautious here?

00:08:42.670 --> 00:08:43.710
Not him.

00:08:44.130 --> 00:08:45.460
Not him, either.

00:08:47.710 --> 00:08:50.280
Time is flowing normally 
for all these people.

00:08:50.890 --> 00:08:52.720
No sign of a Horologue anywhere.

00:08:53.170 --> 00:08:57.720
Does the town's time being reversed 
have nothing to do with a Horologue at all?

00:09:00.000 --> 00:09:03.450
Mina, has anything like 
this happened before?

00:09:03.970 --> 00:09:06.440
If it had, I'd remember it.

00:09:06.440 --> 00:09:08.760
And Chronos would have it on record.

00:09:08.760 --> 00:09:11.420
This is a first, and it makes no sense.

00:09:10.360 --> 00:09:15.370
Twelve plus 27 minus 34... uh...

00:09:15.950 --> 00:09:19.610
<i>If this is Victor's hometown 
34 years in the past,</i>

00:09:20.010 --> 00:09:23.310
<i>then does this phenomenon have 
something to do with him?</i>

00:09:26.120 --> 00:09:30.170
Kiri, this might just be 
some backwoods town to you,

00:09:31.000 --> 00:09:34.350
but for me, it's full of childhood memories.

00:09:34.760 --> 00:09:37.930
Stop looking at these people 
as if they were samples.

00:09:40.260 --> 00:09:41.590
I'm going out for a bit.

00:09:43.710 --> 00:09:45.210
Darling!

00:09:46.690 --> 00:09:48.910
<i>Childhood, huh?</i>

00:09:55.830 --> 00:09:57.280
Very well, then.

00:09:57.670 --> 00:10:01.400
I'll go along with his 
sentimentality a bit longer.

00:10:06.340 --> 00:10:07.740
If nothing else,

00:10:07.740 --> 00:10:11.370
I don't want to be careless and let his
parents discover my relation to Victor.

00:10:11.370 --> 00:10:12.800
That shouldn't be a problem.

00:10:12.800 --> 00:10:15.300
For father and son, you look nothing alike.

00:10:15.300 --> 00:10:17.270
I could say the same to you.

00:10:17.270 --> 00:10:19.780
You look nothing like your sister.

00:10:20.140 --> 00:10:24.190
Of course I don't. We're not real sisters.

00:10:25.460 --> 00:10:29.640
Blood relation to Chronos,
the god of time, is extremely rare,

00:10:29.640 --> 00:10:32.940
so we only call ourselves "sister" 
for the sake of convenience.

00:10:32.940 --> 00:10:36.360
In the first place, I don't 
remember anything from my past.

00:10:36.900 --> 00:10:38.220
Just like my darling.

00:10:38.220 --> 00:10:41.260
You lost your memories, too?
Is that why you...

00:10:41.260 --> 00:10:44.210
Don't get the wrong idea. It's not sympathy.

00:10:44.210 --> 00:10:47.330
I don't care at all that my memory is lost.

00:10:47.720 --> 00:10:50.960
I'm going to build a future with 
my darling, just the two of us.

00:10:51.510 --> 00:10:52.500
That's why this town,

00:10:52.880 --> 00:10:54.040
and every single thing,

00:10:54.170 --> 00:10:55.590
and every single person,

00:10:55.880 --> 00:10:57.090
that ties my darling to his past...

00:10:57.510 --> 00:10:58.680
disgusts me!

00:11:05.670 --> 00:11:07.770
Oh, you're...

00:11:08.270 --> 00:11:11.230
You look pale. Are you all right?

00:11:11.610 --> 00:11:12.920
Come inside.

00:11:15.250 --> 00:11:16.860
What is it, Eve?

00:11:16.860 --> 00:11:18.600
This young man seems unwell.

00:11:18.600 --> 00:11:20.690
What? I'll examine him at once!

00:11:20.690 --> 00:11:24.010
Oh, but I'm seeing another patient now.

00:11:24.010 --> 00:11:26.470
Oh, but there's a patient here, too.

00:11:26.470 --> 00:11:29.320
I'm all right, Doctor Putin.

00:11:29.320 --> 00:11:29.800
Eh?

00:11:29.800 --> 00:11:32.670
I only came to pick up my medicine, anyway.

00:11:33.100 --> 00:11:34.960
How much for the medicine?

00:11:34.960 --> 00:11:37.090
Ah, no, no! I appreciate the thought!

00:11:37.440 --> 00:11:39.590
Just pay it whenever you can.

00:11:39.910 --> 00:11:42.420
Then I'll come again another time.

00:11:43.750 --> 00:11:44.810
Be well...

00:11:46.330 --> 00:11:47.200
Take care.

00:11:52.190 --> 00:11:54.440
My father isn't formally a doctor.

00:11:55.010 --> 00:11:56.910
This town has no hospital,

00:11:56.910 --> 00:11:59.650
which meant people had to travel 
half a day to the next town.

00:12:00.190 --> 00:12:02.560
So he studied medicine on his own time.

00:12:02.560 --> 00:12:04.660
Basically, he's unlicensed.

00:12:05.170 --> 00:12:07.060
His intentions are noble,

00:12:07.060 --> 00:12:10.500
but the fly in the ointment is that he's 
a bit absent-minded and a worrywart.

00:12:10.910 --> 00:12:12.620
Even though he's a doctor?

00:12:12.920 --> 00:12:16.380
The scenery hasn't changed, 
and neither have they.

00:12:16.790 --> 00:12:19.510
My kind, generous mother and father...

00:12:20.570 --> 00:12:22.430
Don't get too sentimental.

00:12:23.850 --> 00:12:25.780
Investigating is our priority now.

00:12:26.240 --> 00:12:29.260
We'll never get your past 
back if we keep this up.

00:12:29.700 --> 00:12:33.480
Twenty-seven minus 34...
That doesn't even work!

00:12:31.390 --> 00:12:33.050
Sentimental, huh?

00:12:33.050 --> 00:12:35.150
Oh, the young man from before.

00:12:35.670 --> 00:12:37.150
How are you feeling?

00:12:37.470 --> 00:12:39.440
Are you all better now?

00:12:42.210 --> 00:12:45.490
What about you? Carrying these heavy 
things when you have a bad heart?

00:12:45.700 --> 00:12:47.180
Is this all right?

00:12:47.180 --> 00:12:49.470
Huh? Yes...

00:12:49.470 --> 00:12:51.500
I need to do at least this much work.

00:12:51.840 --> 00:12:55.250
But what about you? 
Shouldn't you be resting?

00:12:55.250 --> 00:12:58.880
Actually, I am still a bit light-headed...

00:12:57.940 --> 00:12:58.880
Huh?!

00:12:58.880 --> 00:13:01.700
But the place where we're 
staying is just the worst.

00:13:01.700 --> 00:13:03.800
It's got fleas, ticks, lice,

00:13:03.800 --> 00:13:06.950
and roommates that snore and 
toss and turn in their sleep!

00:13:06.950 --> 00:13:10.060
Even worse, we don't even get decent meals.

00:13:10.350 --> 00:13:12.380
Well, that's awful!

00:13:12.380 --> 00:13:15.060
Why don't you come to our 
house for dinner tonight?

00:13:15.360 --> 00:13:17.590
We appreciate your kind offer, but...

00:13:17.590 --> 00:13:19.310
We'd be glad to accept!

00:13:19.310 --> 00:13:19.900
Hey!

00:13:20.660 --> 00:13:23.240
What if they get suspicious 
while we're eating with them?

00:13:23.240 --> 00:13:25.850
Did you forget what I said earlier?

00:13:25.850 --> 00:13:27.360
Of course I haven't.

00:13:27.710 --> 00:13:31.780
Listen, is there anyone more worthy 
of investigation than my parents?

00:13:31.780 --> 00:13:33.290
If we're with them,

00:13:33.510 --> 00:13:36.290
we're sure to figure out 
the cause of all this.

00:13:37.550 --> 00:13:39.030
Yes, but...

00:13:58.610 --> 00:14:01.520
Come to think of it, we haven't 
introduced ourselves.

00:14:01.910 --> 00:14:04.650
My name is Alexander Putin.

00:14:04.650 --> 00:14:07.280
This is my wife, Eve.

00:14:07.560 --> 00:14:09.230
I'm Mina!

00:14:09.230 --> 00:14:11.280
I'm my darling's wife!

00:14:11.580 --> 00:14:14.060
My! As young as you are?

00:14:14.060 --> 00:14:16.810
Love knows no age, remember?

00:14:16.810 --> 00:14:20.230
We were still young when we met, as well.

00:14:20.230 --> 00:14:21.890
That's true.

00:14:23.340 --> 00:14:25.550
Running a health clinic must be difficult.

00:14:25.830 --> 00:14:26.950
Oh, no.

00:14:27.550 --> 00:14:32.640
Actually, I became a doctor in the 
first place because of my wife.

00:14:32.640 --> 00:14:37.540
She has a weak constitution, 
so I wanted to help her.

00:14:37.540 --> 00:14:39.370
I see...

00:14:39.370 --> 00:14:43.400
It's really true that you can do anything 
for the one you love, isn't it?

00:14:43.710 --> 00:14:47.920
I would go through any kind of 
hardship for my darling, too!

00:14:47.920 --> 00:14:49.880
So admirable for one so young!

00:14:49.880 --> 00:14:53.620
Oh, but sir, love knows no age!

00:14:55.320 --> 00:14:57.750
Yes! You're exactly right!

00:14:58.110 --> 00:15:01.670
Whoops! Someone's being left 
out of the conversation.

00:15:01.670 --> 00:15:04.130
Oh, just leave that little prude alone.

00:15:04.790 --> 00:15:08.430
<i>First of all, I'm supposed 
to be one of the guests!</i>

00:15:05.590 --> 00:15:10.470
<b>Thok Thok Thok Thok</b>

00:15:08.430 --> 00:15:10.470
<i>Why am I doing the cooking?!</i>

00:15:10.770 --> 00:15:14.470
<i>Ever since we got here, it's like 
Couljours is messing with me!</i>

00:15:15.490 --> 00:15:16.520
There, it's done!

00:15:19.180 --> 00:15:21.740
It's like we're at a three-star restaurant!

00:15:21.740 --> 00:15:23.940
I'm glad we let him do the cooking!

00:15:24.240 --> 00:15:26.940
I might actually see him in 
a more positive light now.

00:15:27.520 --> 00:15:29.950
Let's eat!

00:15:37.210 --> 00:15:37.890
Huh?

00:15:43.320 --> 00:15:45.110
What did I just eat?!

00:15:45.110 --> 00:15:49.660
Kiri, I forgot that your sense 
of taste is practically absent.

00:15:49.660 --> 00:15:51.180
This is the problem with virgins!

00:15:51.410 --> 00:15:53.390
No, I actually quite like it.

00:15:53.390 --> 00:15:55.680
Though as far as the taste goes, 
it's in unfamiliar territory...

00:15:56.320 --> 00:15:57.440
Dear!

00:15:57.440 --> 00:15:59.180
Hey, you're too loud.

00:15:59.930 --> 00:16:02.510
I'm trying to study, so keep it down!

00:16:03.190 --> 00:16:06.900
Sorry, Victor. We have 
guests here, you see.

00:16:08.460 --> 00:16:10.190
That's my son, Victor.

00:16:10.190 --> 00:16:14.280
Maybe it's not my place to say so, 
but he's been called a prodigy.

00:16:14.280 --> 00:16:15.320
I got it!

00:16:15.320 --> 00:16:18.380
Twelve plus 27 minus 34 equals 5!

00:16:18.380 --> 00:16:19.360
Five years old!

00:16:19.360 --> 00:16:23.020
Huh? Is that wrong? Six? Seven? Eight?

00:16:23.020 --> 00:16:25.170
Yes, he's only five,

00:16:25.380 --> 00:16:27.960
but he's already studying 
at a high school level.

00:16:29.470 --> 00:16:30.330
Wait!

00:16:31.420 --> 00:16:34.320
Take this with you, Vic.

00:16:34.320 --> 00:16:36.030
I made it.

00:16:37.110 --> 00:16:39.470
I don't want it. I'll catch your stupidity.

00:16:39.770 --> 00:16:42.850
Hey, now, Victor!
You shouldn't talk like that!

00:16:42.850 --> 00:16:45.150
Well, it's true, isn't it?

00:16:45.150 --> 00:16:49.450
A weak good-for-nothing who 
can't do anything right,

00:16:49.450 --> 00:16:51.160
and a scatterbrained quack doctor...

00:16:51.550 --> 00:16:55.280
Without my help, you'd have more 
patients dying than getting better.

00:16:56.180 --> 00:16:58.570
I expect nothing of you two.

00:16:58.570 --> 00:16:59.240
Just...

00:16:59.700 --> 00:17:01.940
Don't get in my way.

00:17:02.840 --> 00:17:05.040
You little brat!

00:17:05.580 --> 00:17:08.040
Huh? Why'd you stop me?!

00:17:08.040 --> 00:17:09.470
I'm a villain!

00:17:09.470 --> 00:17:12.690
I'm gonna re-educate that brat but good!

00:17:12.690 --> 00:17:14.180
Calm down, Blaze.

00:17:15.660 --> 00:17:18.500
Just... let it go.

00:17:19.300 --> 00:17:22.000
How can a child be so abusive 
toward his parents?

00:17:22.000 --> 00:17:26.310
It's normal for kids to 
be stupid and impudent.

00:17:35.790 --> 00:17:38.560
What forced Victor to grow up
in the truest sense...

00:17:41.300 --> 00:17:43.310
was the loss of his parents.

00:17:52.090 --> 00:17:52.590
Time Does Not Turn Backward

00:17:53.210 --> 00:17:54.980
Losing them made him realize

00:17:56.470 --> 00:17:58.750
just how precious they were.

00:18:03.600 --> 00:18:05.390
Oh, good morning.

00:18:05.830 --> 00:18:07.940
Thank you for dinner last night.

00:18:08.340 --> 00:18:11.440
Isn't that pen hard to draw with?

00:18:11.720 --> 00:18:12.880
Well, yes.

00:18:13.340 --> 00:18:17.450
But this was a gift from my husband.

00:18:18.660 --> 00:18:21.910
He didn't realize it wasn't an artist's pen.

00:18:22.410 --> 00:18:24.570
But it's not as if I can't draw with it.

00:18:24.570 --> 00:18:28.300
Above all, I have so much 
fun drawing with this pen.

00:18:28.300 --> 00:18:31.310
Yes, I can see that by watching you.

00:18:31.890 --> 00:18:35.050
I hope you all weren't too put off by Vic.

00:18:35.570 --> 00:18:36.320
But—

00:18:38.490 --> 00:18:40.400
Oh, no! You need medicine!

00:18:46.440 --> 00:18:48.940
He's really a very gentle boy.

00:18:49.560 --> 00:18:54.210
Boys his age would normally want to 
play more, or ask for more toys.

00:18:54.210 --> 00:18:56.330
He could be a little more selfish,

00:18:56.330 --> 00:18:58.320
but he helps us with the clinic.

00:18:58.830 --> 00:19:04.740
I'm very proud that Vic has grown 
to be such an independent boy.

00:19:05.430 --> 00:19:07.730
If he seems like a bad boy,

00:19:07.730 --> 00:19:10.110
it's because his father and I 
aren't good enough as parents.

00:19:10.550 --> 00:19:12.350
That's not true at all.

00:19:12.970 --> 00:19:14.750
You're wonderful parents.

00:19:15.880 --> 00:19:19.320
He'll understand that one 
day, too. I'm sure of it.

00:19:20.840 --> 00:19:22.670
Are you going to give that to him?

00:19:22.670 --> 00:19:25.390
Huh? Ah, yes...

00:19:26.060 --> 00:19:30.350
This is the only gift I can give to Vic.

00:19:30.860 --> 00:19:37.190
So I'm hoping to give this 
to him when he turns 20.

00:19:38.070 --> 00:19:40.240
Oh, but please don't.

00:19:40.450 --> 00:19:43.390
Of course. I won't tell him.

00:19:43.910 --> 00:19:44.990
Thank you.

00:19:50.200 --> 00:19:52.330
You've had enough sentimentality, right?

00:19:52.900 --> 00:19:54.920
Or are you trying to atone?

00:19:55.670 --> 00:19:58.210
Your parents died in a fire.

00:19:58.210 --> 00:20:00.230
The cause remains unknown even now.

00:20:00.230 --> 00:20:04.090
All we know is that Eve collapsed 
due to her weak heart

00:20:04.090 --> 00:20:05.910
and couldn't get out in time,

00:20:06.780 --> 00:20:10.160
so Alex did his best to 
go back and save her.

00:20:10.160 --> 00:20:13.940
In the end, you never received 
that drawing from your mother.

00:20:15.220 --> 00:20:16.200
Right?

00:20:17.750 --> 00:20:21.320
Do you intend to get that drawing 
and thank her personally?

00:20:23.980 --> 00:20:28.450
I already know what she's drawing.

00:20:39.220 --> 00:20:43.320
It was a wish from my awkward parents

00:20:43.320 --> 00:20:46.150
for me to "be a victor."

00:20:51.580 --> 00:20:54.410
Kiri, you don't yet understand

00:20:54.840 --> 00:20:56.770
how parents feel about their children.

00:20:57.120 --> 00:20:59.210
It's not something that 
can be easily explained.

00:20:59.770 --> 00:21:01.200
Wait, Victor!

00:21:01.200 --> 00:21:03.860
The parents in front of you now are fakes!

00:21:03.860 --> 00:21:05.310
The past can't be changed!

00:21:05.310 --> 00:21:07.660
No matter what you do for them now,
it'll mean nothing!

00:21:08.360 --> 00:21:10.170
It sounds good to say you're atoning,

00:21:10.170 --> 00:21:11.460
but it's only for your own satisfac—

00:21:11.460 --> 00:21:12.730
Shut up, Kiri.

00:21:16.320 --> 00:21:19.470
You don't understand anything, Kiri.

00:21:20.870 --> 00:21:22.560
Investigating is fine.

00:21:22.890 --> 00:21:26.260
But we'll work separately. 
There's something I need to do.

00:21:38.170 --> 00:21:40.690
Victor!

00:21:42.120 --> 00:21:42.960
Damn it!

00:21:51.410 --> 00:21:51.490
Fact and Fiction

00:21:51.490 --> 00:21:54.700
Fact and Fiction

00:21:54.700 --> 00:21:54.750
Fact and Fiction

00:21:54.790 --> 00:21:54.830
Fact and Fiction

00:21:54.870 --> 00:21:54.910
Fact and Fiction

